germany: 1000A-1018 answered HTTP 400 Bad Request ('<html>\n<head>\n<base href="/error_path/">\n<title>400 Bad Request</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<h1>Bad Request</h1>\n<p>The server detected a syntax error in your request.<br>\nCheck your request and all parameters.</p>\n\n<p>Your request ID was: arkaX9Ha1c8l_cyD5I7RkQAAAwg</p>\n\n\n                                                                                                    \n                                                                                                    \n                                                                                                    \n                            '). A 401 here means the account was not accepted -- this API reads the credential from the request headers and ignores it as a query parameter, so a working account presented the wrong way looks exactly like a rejected one.
